## Implemented
- Initial absent-destination publication uses parent-directory-descriptor-anchored Darwin renameatx_np RENAME_EXCL or Linux renameat2 RENAME_NOREPLACE. A raced foreign destination is preserved by inode and publication fails closed.
- Archive verification opens once with O_NOFOLLOW and a 32 MiB fstat cap, hashes and rewinds the same file object, then performs bounded exact USTAR parsing without getmembers or unbounded hostile metadata allocation.
- sha256_file, archive parsing, and write_new_file_at retain descriptor ownership until fdopen succeeds and close on injected conversion failure. Output mode changes use fchmod.
